@*
    TokenRenderer — renders accumulated text from TextDelta chunks.

    Each new TextDelta chunk is appended as a <span> with the "bumper-pulse"
    CSS animation class so the user sees new tokens "land" on the surface in a
    pinball-themed way. The animation completes quickly (300ms) and is not
    distracting on subsequent renders.

    Accessibility / prefers-reduced-motion:
      • When the user's OS has reduced-motion enabled, no animation is applied —
        the span is rendered statically. The CSS media query gates this.
      • The containing element uses role="region" + aria-live="polite" so
        screen readers announce accumulated text as it arrives.

    Rendering contract:
      • SpanTexts is the ordered list of delta strings. Each delta gets its own
        <span> with a CSS class for the animation. Accumulated spans together
        form the answer prose.
      • When Final arrives, the parent replaces SpanTexts with the canonical
        answer text from Final.Answer.Text split into a single span (or a cleared
        list + the full text in one span). This is handled by the parent
        WizardAnswerStream — TokenRenderer just renders whatever it receives.
      • Markdown rendering: during streaming (IsStreaming=true) the plain-text
        span path is used unchanged — deltas can split mid-marker so formatting
        must be deferred. When IsStreaming=false (Final has landed or historical
        turn) the canonical single-span text is passed to MarkdownContent which
        renders bold/italic/lists via MarkdownTokenizer. The streaming hot path
        is completely untouched by this change.

    Category: delight surface (within WizardAnswerStream scope per ADR-0026
    § 6). Custom CSS animation component — within the locked set.

    ADR-0026 § 3, § 5 — streaming; Final supersedes TextDelta
    ADR-0008          — MudBlazor strict for chrome; TokenRenderer is a custom
                        delight-surface sub-component of WizardAnswerStream
*@

@if (SpanTexts.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="token-renderer"
         data-testid="token-renderer"
         role="region"
         aria-live="polite"
         aria-label="Answer text">
        @if (IsStreaming)
        {
            @* Streaming path: plain-text spans with bumper-pulse animation.
               Deltas may split mid-marker ("**Godz" + "illa**") so markdown
               formatting is deferred until Final. Hot path — no change here. *@
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="token-renderer__text">
                @foreach (var (text, index) in SpanTexts.Select((t, i) => (t, i)))
                {
                    @* The "bumper-pulse" class triggers the entry animation.
                       Only apply it to the last span (the most recently arrived
                       delta) so prior spans are stable and don't re-animate on
                       re-render. *@
                    var isNewest = index == SpanTexts.Count - 1;
                    <span class="@(isNewest ? "token-renderer__span token-renderer__span--new" : "token-renderer__span")"
                          data-testid="token-span">@text</span>
                }
            </MudText>
        }
        else
        {
            @* Canonical path (Final landed or historical turn): render through
               MarkdownContent so bold/italic/list syntax becomes real markup.
               SpanTexts is a single-entry list at this point (Final.Answer.Text).
               Join the entries to handle the edge case where the parent passes
               multiple spans in non-streaming mode (shouldn't happen, but
               defensive). *@
            <MarkdownContent Text="@string.Join(string.Empty, SpanTexts)" />
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    // Ordered list of text delta strings. Each entry was yielded by a
    // separate TextDelta chunk. The parent accumulates these and passes
    // the full list so TokenRenderer renders them as one run of spans.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> SpanTexts { get; set; } = [];

    // True while chunks are still arriving (Streaming / CitationsArriving
    // state). Controls whether the newest span gets the bumper-pulse class.
    // Set to false once Final arrives so the last span doesn't re-animate
    // during state machine transition to Complete.
    [Parameter]
    public bool IsStreaming { get; set; }
}
